  "question": {
    "text": "A pulley of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is rotated about its axis by a force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>20</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> newton (where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is measured in seconds) applied tangentially. If the moment of inertia of the pulley about its axis of rotation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the number of rotation made by the pulley before its direction of motion is reversed is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "more than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> but less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "more than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> but less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "more than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,</p><p>Torque <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>20</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>But <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;so</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Integrating&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math> will&nbsp;be&nbsp;zero&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Again, integrating both sides<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>since. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>so, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p>Number of turns, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>73</mn></math></p>"
  }
}